    <item ident="gc80bce55f715194f2eeeac2e46e865a3" title="Question 1">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>56973,87235,13875,34331</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is plagiarism?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="56973">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Presenting someone else's words, ideas, or creative work as your own</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="87235">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using quotation marks to credit a source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="13875">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Writing a summary of a source in your own words</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="34331">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking a classmate to review your draft for feedback</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">87235</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="87235_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">13875</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="13875_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">34331</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="34331_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">56973</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="87235_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Plagiarism is not a citation method or a form of feedback. It is presenting another person's words, ideas, or creative work as your own, whether or not the act is intentional. Using quotation marks and citing a source is the opposite of plagiarism—it is proper attribution. Writing a summary in your own words with a citation is also acceptable. Asking a classmate for feedback, without having them rewrite your work, is a permitted form of collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="13875_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Plagiarism is not a citation method or a form of feedback. It is presenting another person's words, ideas, or creative work as your own, whether or not the act is intentional. Using quotation marks and citing a source is the opposite of plagiarism—it is proper attribution. Writing a summary in your own words with a citation is also acceptable. Asking a classmate for feedback, without having them rewrite your work, is a permitted form of collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="34331_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Plagiarism is not a citation method or a form of feedback. It is presenting another person's words, ideas, or creative work as your own, whether or not the act is intentional. Using quotation marks and citing a source is the opposite of plagiarism—it is proper attribution. Writing a summary in your own words with a citation is also acceptable. Asking a classmate for feedback, without having them rewrite your work, is a permitted form of collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g02622b04afd55aa56f598923d3f6d853" title="Question 10">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>69449,563,67760,8535</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is contract cheating?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="69449">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Paying or trading favors for someone else to complete an assignment</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="563">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using an online grammar checker to correct punctuation errors</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="67760">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking a family member to encourage you while you write</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="8535">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Submitting a draft before the deadline to receive early feedback</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">563</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="563_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">67760</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="67760_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">8535</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="8535_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69449</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="563_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Contract cheating occurs when a student pays or trades favors for someone else to complete an assignment on their behalf. Using a grammar checker is a tool-based editing aid and is not cheating. Receiving encouragement from a family member is a welcome form of support in WRIT 101, as long as the family member does not write or rewrite the work. Submitting a draft early for instructor feedback is an appropriate academic behavior, not a violation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="67760_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Contract cheating occurs when a student pays or trades favors for someone else to complete an assignment on their behalf. Using a grammar checker is a tool-based editing aid and is not cheating. Receiving encouragement from a family member is a welcome form of support in WRIT 101, as long as the family member does not write or rewrite the work. Submitting a draft early for instructor feedback is an appropriate academic behavior, not a violation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="8535_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Contract cheating occurs when a student pays or trades favors for someone else to complete an assignment on their behalf. Using a grammar checker is a tool-based editing aid and is not cheating. Receiving encouragement from a family member is a welcome form of support in WRIT 101, as long as the family member does not write or rewrite the work. Submitting a draft early for instructor feedback is an appropriate academic behavior, not a violation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g1605251d125e9e2eef81c103ca89206d" title="Question 11">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>78913,84960,95580,11632</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is direct plagiarism?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="78913">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Copying another person's exact words without quotation marks or a citation</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="84960">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Restating a source's main idea in your own words without a citation</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="95580">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Submitting a personal essay you wrote for a previous course</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="11632">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using AI to generate a reference list for your assignment</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">84960</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="84960_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">95580</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="95580_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">11632</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="11632_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">78913</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="84960_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Direct plagiarism means copying another person's exact words and presenting them as your own without quotation marks or a source citation. Restating a source's main idea without a citation is a different violation called insufficient citation. Submitting previously completed work is self-plagiarism, not direct plagiarism. Using AI to generate a reference list without verifying the sources is fabrication, which is a separate integrity issue.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="95580_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Direct plagiarism means copying another person's exact words and presenting them as your own without quotation marks or a source citation. Restating a source's main idea without a citation is a different violation called insufficient citation. Submitting previously completed work is self-plagiarism, not direct plagiarism. Using AI to generate a reference list without verifying the sources is fabrication, which is a separate integrity issue.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="11632_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Direct plagiarism means copying another person's exact words and presenting them as your own without quotation marks or a source citation. Restating a source's main idea without a citation is a different violation called insufficient citation. Submitting previously completed work is self-plagiarism, not direct plagiarism. Using AI to generate a reference list without verifying the sources is fabrication, which is a separate integrity issue.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="ga0e4904e654287d1070eb44da0f6a83a" title="Question 12">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>85048,33984,97691,60782</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What does the Explainability Test require a student to do?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="85048">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Confirm that they can explain what they submitted and could produce it again independently</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="33984">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Provide a written explanation of every source used in the assignment</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="97691">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Share all AI conversation transcripts with the instructor before submitting</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="60782">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Explain the assignment requirements to a classmate before beginning</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">33984</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="33984_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">97691</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="97691_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">60782</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="60782_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">85048</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="33984_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The Explainability Test asks two questions: Can you explain what you submitted to someone else, and could you do it again on your own? If the answers are no, AI completed the task for you rather than helping you learn. Providing a written explanation of sources is a citation practice, not the Explainability Test. Transcripts may be requested by an instructor, but sharing them before submission is not the definition of the test. Explaining requirements to a classmate is not part of this integrity standard.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="97691_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The Explainability Test asks two questions: Can you explain what you submitted to someone else, and could you do it again on your own? If the answers are no, AI completed the task for you rather than helping you learn. Providing a written explanation of sources is a citation practice, not the Explainability Test. Transcripts may be requested by an instructor, but sharing them before submission is not the definition of the test. Explaining requirements to a classmate is not part of this integrity standard.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="60782_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The Explainability Test asks two questions: Can you explain what you submitted to someone else, and could you do it again on your own? If the answers are no, AI completed the task for you rather than helping you learn. Providing a written explanation of sources is a citation practice, not the Explainability Test. Transcripts may be requested by an instructor, but sharing them before submission is not the definition of the test. Explaining requirements to a classmate is not part of this integrity standard.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g1e0e1c2e599d3872e899b0e4f9e1dbff" title="Question 13">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>76065,36164,20629,12400</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;Which of the following describes a feedback prompt when using AI?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="76065">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to identify problems in your writing without rewriting anything</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="36164">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to rewrite a paragraph to improve its clarity</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="20629">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI tochoose which details to include in your personal narrative</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="12400">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to improve the overall tone of your essay</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">36164</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="36164_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">20629</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="20629_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">12400</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="12400_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">76065</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="36164_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A feedback prompt asks AI to identify a problem while leaving all decisions and revisions to the student. Asking AI to rewrite a paragraph, select story details, or improve your tone are edit requests — they transfer the intellectual work of the assignment from the student to the AI. The key distinction is this: feedback prompts keep the work with you, while edit requests remove the work from you.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="20629_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A feedback prompt asks AI to identify a problem while leaving all decisions and revisions to the student. Asking AI to rewrite a paragraph, select story details, or improve your tone are edit requests — they transfer the intellectual work of the assignment from the student to the AI. The key distinction is this: feedback prompts keep the work with you, while edit requests remove the work from you.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="12400_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A feedback prompt asks AI to identify a problem while leaving all decisions and revisions to the student. Asking AI to rewrite a paragraph, select story details, or improve your tone are edit requests — they transfer the intellectual work of the assignment from the student to the AI. The key distinction is this: feedback prompts keep the work with you, while edit requests remove the work from you.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g369a41dbf61c706e77b69f6acba4a7a5" title="Question 14">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
