    <item ident="g3b36173cc76ff0f141185b5216bad573" title="Question 22">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>28082,75366,84938,26652</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What does it mean to provide "insufficient citation" in academic writing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="28082">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using another person's idea in your own words without crediting the source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="75366">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Formatting a citation incorrectly in the reference list</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="84938">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Including fewer sources than recommended in a research assignment</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="26652">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using a source that is not listed in the course reading materials</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">75366</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="75366_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">84938</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="84938_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">26652</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="26652_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">28082</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="75366_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Insufficient citation means using another person's idea or argument—even in your own words—without providing credit to the original source. The idea belongs to its originator regardless of how it is expressed. Formatting a citation incorrectly is a citation style error, not the same as insufficient citation. Using too few sources is a research depth issue. Using a source outside the assigned readings is permitted as long as it is properly cited.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="84938_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Insufficient citation means using another person's idea or argument—even in your own words—without providing credit to the original source. The idea belongs to its originator regardless of how it is expressed. Formatting a citation incorrectly is a citation style error, not the same as insufficient citation. Using too few sources is a research depth issue. Using a source outside the assigned readings is permitted as long as it is properly cited.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="26652_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Insufficient citation means using another person's idea or argument—even in your own words—without providing credit to the original source. The idea belongs to its originator regardless of how it is expressed. Formatting a citation incorrectly is a citation style error, not the same as insufficient citation. Using too few sources is a research depth issue. Using a source outside the assigned readings is permitted as long as it is properly cited.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gfd981bef3c75be53f79f8c12cace3744" title="Question 23">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>8820,37182,88879,97039</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What does it mean to falsify information in academic writing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="8820">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Misrepresenting real information</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="37182">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Creating entirely new information that never existed</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="88879">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Quoting a source out of context</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="97039">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Failing to include a citation for a paraphrased idea</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">37182</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="37182_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">88879</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="88879_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">97039</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="97039_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">8820</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="37182_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Falsification means misrepresenting real information—for example, changing what a family member actually said in an interview. Creating entirely new false information is fabrication, which is a related but distinct violation. Quoting out of context is a misuse of sources but is not the standard definition of falsification. Failing to cite a paraphrased idea is insufficient citation, not falsification.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="88879_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Falsification means misrepresenting real information—for example, changing what a family member actually said in an interview. Creating entirely new false information is fabrication, which is a related but distinct violation. Quoting out of context is a misuse of sources but is not the standard definition of falsification. Failing to cite a paraphrased idea is insufficient citation, not falsification.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="97039_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Falsification means misrepresenting real information—for example, changing what a family member actually said in an interview. Creating entirely new false information is fabrication, which is a related but distinct violation. Quoting out of context is a misuse of sources but is not the standard definition of falsification. Failing to cite a paraphrased idea is insufficient citation, not falsification.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gc6c668b11400f24692a6c7b929d8798c" title="Question 24">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>69105,95942,22215,56579</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is content sharing in the context of academic integrity?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="69105">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Distributing completed assignments to other students or obtaining completed assignments from others</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="95942">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Posting your own essay on a personal blog that is not shared with classmates</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="22215">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Discussing assignment topics with classmates before beginning to write</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="56579">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reading a classmate's published work for inspiration</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">95942</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="95942_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">22215</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="22215_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">56579</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="56579_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69105</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="95942_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Content sharing violations occur when a student distributes completed work to others or obtains completed work from others. Both the person sharing and the person receiving are equally responsible. Posting your own essay on a personal blog is not considered content sharing if other classmates will not be able to access it. Discussing topics with classmates before writing is a normal pre-writing behavior. Reading a classmate's published work for inspiration, without copying it, is not a sharing violation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="22215_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Content sharing violations occur when a student distributes completed work to others or obtains completed work from others. Both the person sharing and the person receiving are equally responsible. Posting your own essay on a personal blog is not considered content sharing if other classmates will not be able to access it. Discussing topics with classmates before writing is a normal pre-writing behavior. Reading a classmate's published work for inspiration, without copying it, is not a sharing violation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="56579_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Content sharing violations occur when a student distributes completed work to others or obtains completed work from others. Both the person sharing and the person receiving are equally responsible. Posting your own essay on a personal blog is not considered content sharing if other classmates will not be able to access it. Discussing topics with classmates before writing is a normal pre-writing behavior. Reading a classmate's published work for inspiration, without copying it, is not a sharing violation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g66073ee494e9f74fccf366c416f00d4b" title="Question 25">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
