    <item ident="gfbc6f0adffe7c182ba4fa69ff7a90158" title="Question 26">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>44072,64457,36674,18704</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is the "thesaurus method," and why is it a problem?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="44072">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It replaces individual words in a source with synonyms while keeping the original structure, which is still plagiarism.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="64457">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It is an approved technique for paraphrasing that uses a dictionary to find alternative words while maintaining meaning.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="36674">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It is a method for summarizing sources by reducing them to key vocabulary terms while preserving main ideas.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="18704">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It is a citation format that lists only the most important words from a source title for reference purposes.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">64457</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="64457_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">36674</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="36674_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">18704</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="18704_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">44072</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="64457_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The thesaurus method refers to swapping individual words in a source for synonyms without changing the sentence structure. This is still plagiarism because the original structure and ideas remain unchanged, even when a citation is included. True paraphrasing requires expressing the idea in both your own words and your own sentence structure. The thesaurus method is not an approved paraphrasing technique, a summarizing method, or a citation format.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="36674_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The thesaurus method refers to swapping individual words in a source for synonyms without changing the sentence structure. This is still plagiarism because the original structure and ideas remain unchanged, even when a citation is included. True paraphrasing requires expressing the idea in both your own words and your own sentence structure. The thesaurus method is not an approved paraphrasing technique, a summarizing method, or a citation format.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="18704_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The thesaurus method refers to swapping individual words in a source for synonyms without changing the sentence structure. This is still plagiarism because the original structure and ideas remain unchanged, even when a citation is included. True paraphrasing requires expressing the idea in both your own words and your own sentence structure. The thesaurus method is not an approved paraphrasing technique, a summarizing method, or a citation format.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
