      <itemfeedback ident="95137_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Every source in a reference list must be a real publication that the student has located and read. This requirement exists because AI can generate citations that appear correctly formatted but refer to publications that do not exist. Including a direct quotation is not required for every source. Summarizing and paraphrasing are also valid. Instructor approval is not required before using a source. Finding a confirming second source is a research quality practice but is not the requirement stated in this module.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
