    <item ident="gbd9745397573715cd86289bffe3f55ae" title="Question 32">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>15283,51127,13370,29878</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is the purpose of the AI disclosure statement required at the top of every WRIT 101 assignment?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="15283">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To inform the instructor whether AI was used and in what specific way.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="51127">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To give the student permission to use AI on the assignment.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="13370">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To confirm that the student has read the course syllabus.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="29878">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To record the name of the AI tool for the instructor's research purposes.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">51127</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="51127_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">13370</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="13370_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">29878</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="29878_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">15283</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="51127_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The disclosure statement exists so the instructor knows whether AI was used and, if so, exactly what function it served. It is a transparency requirement, not a permission grant. The student's agreement to course policies is separate from the disclosure statement. The statement is not collected for research—it is an integrity requirement tied directly to honest submission of academic work.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="13370_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The disclosure statement exists so the instructor knows whether AI was used and, if so, exactly what function it served. It is a transparency requirement, not a permission grant. The student's agreement to course policies is separate from the disclosure statement. The statement is not collected for research—it is an integrity requirement tied directly to honest submission of academic work.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
