    <item ident="g8ebe9d08c99fb6e84ac39a1a720dcb37" title="Question 35">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>71459,31097,69689,73973</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the approved use of AI when a student is uncertain about how to integrate a quotation into their writing?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="71459">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Ask AI to explain the technique, then apply it independently using the student's own source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="31097">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Ask AI to write a sample sentence integrating the quotation correctly</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="69689">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Ask AI to rewrite the paragraph so the quotation fits naturally</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="73973">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Ask AI to select a better quotation from the same source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">31097</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="31097_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69689</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="69689_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">73973</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="73973_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">71459</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="31097_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The approved method is to ask AI to explain the technique and then apply it yourself. This builds competence because the student does the intellectual work. Asking AI to write a sample sentence, rewrite the paragraph, or select a quotation all transfer the work to AI instead of developing the student's own ability. The principle of developing competence requires the student to perform the work independently after receiving an explanation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="69689_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The approved method is to ask AI to explain the technique and then apply it yourself. This builds competence because the student does the intellectual work. Asking AI to write a sample sentence, rewrite the paragraph, or select a quotation all transfer the work to AI instead of developing the student's own ability. The principle of developing competence requires the student to perform the work independently after receiving an explanation.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
