    <item ident="g508191e1d79304992e10824a14ef07f1" title="Question 6">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>94462,25614,45387,53272</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is self-plagiarism?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="94462">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Submitting work you previously submitted for another course or assignment without instructor permission</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="25614">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Repeating your own ideas more than once within a single essay</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="45387">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Writing about personal experiences that are similar to a published author's experiences</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="53272">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using the same thesis statement in two different paragraphs</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">25614</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="25614_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">45387</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="45387_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">53272</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="53272_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">94462</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="25614_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Self-plagiarism means submitting work that was previously submitted in another class or context without your instructor's permission. Repeating ideas within a single essay is a writing style issue, not an integrity violation.Writing about personal experiences that overlap with a published author's does not constitute self-plagiarism. Using the same thesis in two paragraphs is not an academic honesty violation. In fact, it is both acceptable and often effective to restate your thesis statement, especially in the conclusion of your essay, to reinforce your main argument.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45387_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Self-plagiarism means submitting work that was previously submitted in another class or context without your instructor's permission. Repeating ideas within a single essay is a writing style issue, not an integrity violation.Writing about personal experiences that overlap with a published author's does not constitute self-plagiarism. Using the same thesis in two paragraphs is not an academic honesty violation. In fact, it is both acceptable and often effective to restate your thesis statement, especially in the conclusion of your essay, to reinforce your main argument.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="53272_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Self-plagiarism means submitting work that was previously submitted in another class or context without your instructor's permission. Repeating ideas within a single essay is a writing style issue, not an integrity violation.Writing about personal experiences that overlap with a published author's does not constitute self-plagiarism. Using the same thesis in two paragraphs is not an academic honesty violation. In fact, it is both acceptable and often effective to restate your thesis statement, especially in the conclusion of your essay, to reinforce your main argument.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g64bfe5c296f0caa7d4f150e1ca6bb89e" title="Question 7">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>55173,77780,42603,27458</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;Which of the following is an appropriate way to use AI in WRIT 101?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="55173">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to explain the difference between summarizing and paraphrasing</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="77780">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to write a first draft of your personal narrative</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="42603">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to decide which story details to include in your essay</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="27458">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to rewrite a paragraph to make it clearer</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">77780</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="77780_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">42603</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="42603_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">27458</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="27458_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">55173</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="77780_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to explain a concept, such as the difference between summarizing and paraphrasing, is an approved use because it builds your understanding without replacing your work. Asking AI to write your draft, select your story details, or rewrite your paragraphs are all inappropriate uses. Each of those actions transfers the intellectual and creative work of the assignment from you to the AI, which violates both course policy and the principle of competence development.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="42603_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to explain a concept, such as the difference between summarizing and paraphrasing, is an approved use because it builds your understanding without replacing your work. Asking AI to write your draft, select your story details, or rewrite your paragraphs are all inappropriate uses. Each of those actions transfers the intellectual and creative work of the assignment from you to the AI, which violates both course policy and the principle of competence development.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="27458_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking AI to explain a concept, such as the difference between summarizing and paraphrasing, is an approved use because it builds your understanding without replacing your work. Asking AI to write your draft, select your story details, or rewrite your paragraphs are all inappropriate uses. Each of those actions transfers the intellectual and creative work of the assignment from you to the AI, which violates both course policy and the principle of competence development.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g538ec4886f1cd1ff118fa0753da52c87" title="Question 8">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
