    <item ident="g42836d868b25b4b639e3623aa94ca1bc" title="Question 9">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>81674,52485,65235,1061</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is a process task?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="81674">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">An assignment where the goal is to build a skill, not just produce a finished document</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="52485">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">An assignment focused on following instructions exactly rather than developing understanding</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="65235">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A task where AI assistance is always permitted</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="1061">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">An assignment that focuses on producing a clean, usable result</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">52485</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="52485_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">65235</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="65235_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">1061</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="1061_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">81674</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="52485_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A process task is one where learning and skill development is the purpose. The document you produce is not the end goal—developing the ability to produce it is. An assignment that emphasizes following instructions or completing steps correctly focuses on execution rather than learning, and therefore does not reflect a process task as defined in this module. AI assistance is not automatically permitted on process tasks; major writing assignments in WRIT 101 are process tasks where AI use is significantly restricted. An assignment focused on producing a clean, usable result is a product task, which is the opposite of a process task.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="65235_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A process task is one where learning and skill development is the purpose. The document you produce is not the end goal—developing the ability to produce it is. An assignment that emphasizes following instructions or completing steps correctly focuses on execution rather than learning, and therefore does not reflect a process task as defined in this module. AI assistance is not automatically permitted on process tasks; major writing assignments in WRIT 101 are process tasks where AI use is significantly restricted. An assignment focused on producing a clean, usable result is a product task, which is the opposite of a process task.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="1061_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A process task is one where learning and skill development is the purpose. The document you produce is not the end goal—developing the ability to produce it is. An assignment that emphasizes following instructions or completing steps correctly focuses on execution rather than learning, and therefore does not reflect a process task as defined in this module. AI assistance is not automatically permitted on process tasks; major writing assignments in WRIT 101 are process tasks where AI use is significantly restricted. An assignment focused on producing a clean, usable result is a product task, which is the opposite of a process task.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
